      "matchText": "Shugei Shuchiin",
      "term": "Shugei Shuchiin",
      "definition": "The first school in Japanese history open to commoners, founded by Kukai in 828 near his temple Toji in the capital. Unlike the existing schools that trained only aristocrats and officials, it admitted students regardless of birth and fed them for free — a strikingly egalitarian experiment that did not long outlive its founder."
