      "matchText": "Ike no Zenni",
      "term": "Ike no Zenni",
      "definition": "Taira no Kiyomori's stepmother, a Heian-period noblewoman. After the Heiji Disturbance she begged Kiyomori to spare the captured boy Yoritomo — reportedly because he resembled a son of hers who had died young — and so set in motion the Minamoto revival that would later destroy the Taira."
    },
    {
      "matchText": "Holy Land",
      "term": "Holy Land",
      "definition": "The region around Jerusalem held sacred by Jews, Christians, and Muslims. In the 1180s it was the battleground between the Crusader states and Saladin's reunified Muslim forces, who retook Jerusalem in 1187."
    },
    {
      "matchText": "Crusaders",
      "term": "Crusaders",
      "definition": "Western European Christian warriors who, from 1095 onward, fought to seize and hold the Holy Land. They had carved out states around Jerusalem in the early twelfth century, only to lose the city to Saladin in 1187."
    }
